{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{# Specific context for the main narrative of Section 6 (EOP Deep Dive) #}
{# NOTE: Correcting the likely error in REPORT_STRUCTURE which might have listed section3_narrative.j2 #}
{% set output_format_description = "a coherent narrative paragraph (or potentially two short paragraphs) summarizing the analysis of EOP vulnerabilities, suitable for the main body text. Use Markdown for clarity (e.g., simple bolding) if helpful." %}

{% block task_instructions %}
Synthesize the provided chart insights, callouts, and data summaries for "{{ section_title }}" into a flowing narrative text focused specifically on Elevation of Privilege (EOP) vulnerabilities.
Your narrative should cover:
1. The trend in the proportion of EOP vulnerabilities relative to all CVEs during the reporting period.
2. The distribution of attack vectors most commonly associated with these EOP vulnerabilities and what that implies (e.g., often requires initial local access).
Integrate the key points highlighted in the callouts. Aim for 3-6 sentences. You may use simple Markdown (like **bold**) for emphasis if appropriate.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Section Key: {{ data_context_payload.section_key | default('section_6_eop_deep_dive') }}

Chart Insights Generated for this Section:
{% for chart_id, insight in data_context_payload.chart_insights_in_section.items() %}
- Insight ({{ chart_id }}): {{ insight }}
{% else %}
- No specific chart insights provided.
{% endfor %}

Callouts Generated for this Section:
{% for callout_key, callout_text in data_context_payload.callouts_in_section.items() %}
- {{ callout_key | replace("_", " ") | title }}: {{ callout_text }}
{% else %}
- No callouts generated for this section.
{% endfor %}

Data Summaries for Charts in this Section:
{% for chart_id, summary in data_context_payload.charts_data_summaries_in_section.items() %}
--- Data Summary: {{ chart_id }} ---
{{ summary }}
--- End Summary ---
{% else %}
- No chart data summaries provided.
{% endfor %}
{% endblock data_context %}
